This walkthrough covers the **Magic board** version, which is the latest: your `index.html`, `style.css` and `index.js` in the `magic-board/` folder, including the shapes I added. The infinite-canvas app and the plain tutorial copy are separate projects, and I can explain either one in the same way.

# The big picture

The page has three files with separate jobs:
- **`index.html`** is the structure: a header with tool buttons and a canvas.
- **`style.css`** is the look.
- **`index.js`** is the behavior. It reads mouse input and paints pixels onto the `<canvas>`.

The app keeps no list of strokes. Whatever you draw is just pixels on the canvas, which is why you can't move or delete a stroke afterwards.

