# 2. style.css

**Setup**
- **`@import`** loads the Dosis font from Google Fonts.
- **`:root`** defines four custom properties, which are reusable values: `--font-main`, `--ink` (the navy text color), `--line` (light borders) and `--page` (the grey page background).

**Page and header**
- **`body`** removes the default margin and padding and sets the font, text color and grey background. `box-sizing: border-box` is set here but has no real effect, because that property isn't inherited by child elements.
- **`header`** is `width: 90%` with `margin: 0 auto` to center it. `padding: 8px 5%` adds 5% on each side, so the bar fills 100% of the width in total. It's a flex container (`display: flex`) with `justify-content: space-between` to push the title left and the tools right, and `align-items: center` to line them up vertically. The background, border and shadow are cosmetic.
- **`header h2`** removes the heading's default margin and makes it bolder.
- **`.tools`** is a flex row with a 20px `gap`. `flex-wrap: wrap` (my addition) lets the buttons drop to a second line on narrow screens.

**Palette**
- **`.color-palette`** is a CSS grid with 10 columns of 18px and a 5px gap, so 20 swatches form two rows.
- **`.color`** makes each swatch 18×18px with a border and rounded corners. `background-color: var(--set-color)` reads the color from each span's own inline style, which is why one rule can paint 20 different colors. The `.color:hover` rule enlarges a swatch slightly when you point at it.

**Canvas**
- **`.canvas-container`** sets the height to 90% of the viewport and adds 10px of padding on every side. That padding is why `resize()` subtracts 20 from the width. Its `cursor` property uses your pencil image, with `auto` as the fallback.
- **`canvas`** is `display: block`, which removes a small gap browsers leave under inline images. The white background, border and rounded corners are CSS only. They are not part of the pixels, so saved PNGs stay transparent.

**Buttons**
- **`.btn`** gives every button the same font, border, rounded corners and a pointer cursor. `position: relative` makes the button the anchor for the size dropdown. `.btn:hover` shades it slightly.
- **`.color-btn`** and **`.color-btn div`** make the color button 50px wide and stretch the preview box across it. The `background-color: green` is only a placeholder, because JavaScript replaces it.
- **`.size-btn`** and **`.size-btn span`** add padding and spacing around the "Size" text.

**Size dropdown**
- **`.size-list`** is the dropdown panel. `display: none` hides it, and `position: absolute` places it relative to the button. `top: 100%` puts it right under the button, `margin-top: 6px` adds a gap and `z-index: 2` keeps it above the canvas. The rest is styling: white background, shadow and a column layout that centers the bars.
- **`.show-list`** sets `display: flex`. JavaScript adds and removes this class to open and close the list.
- **`.size-list li`** and **`.size-list li div`** make each bar 85% of the list's width. `height: var(--set-size)` gives the bar its own thickness.

**Hidden color input**
- **`input[type=color]`** is invisible (`opacity: 0`, `visibility: hidden`) and moved out of the layout, but it still works because the label triggers it.

**Shapes (new)**
- **`.shapes`** lines up the shape buttons in a row. `.shape-btn` gives them a fixed size and centers the icon. `.btn.active` highlights the selected tool. `.fill-label` styles the Fill checkbox and its text.

